The main improvement is replacing the single-level conditional partition with a bounded recursive prefix tree. Values are factorized once per column, and each tree node selects a repeated field using the required length-weighted `count * (count - 1)` objective. Recursion is capped at depth three, candidate columns are capped at sixteen per node, and total row memberships processed are capped at `4*n`, preventing the timeout seen in the earlier implementation.

The exact serialized Trie objective still selects among the global and conditional candidates, so the heuristic cannot replace a better candidate.

